WEBVTT - Upgrade planning and migration: agent skills for TYPO3 (en)

1
00:00:02.040 --> 00:00:07.120
How long will the upgrade take, and what happens
when a step goes wrong?

2
00:00:08.220 --> 00:00:14.816
Upgrade planning and migration: four skills for
TYPO3 v14.

3
00:00:16.116 --> 00:00:23.704
Estimates an LTS upgrade per extension, with
risk multipliers for the v14 breaking changes.

4
00:00:25.054 --> 00:00:34.497
A number per extension is easier to plan with
than a gut feeling, and it shows how much Rector
saves: 15 to 20 per cent.

5
00:00:35.897 --> 00:00:45.209
Moves a deployed project to a new LTS: site
configuration, TypoScript, templates, Docker and
database.

6
00:00:46.559 --> 00:00:52.292
It covers the project; typo3-extension-upgrade
covers extension code.

7
00:00:53.692 --> 00:01:02.430
Carries out one migration step behind a rollback
point: Composer, Rector, Fractor, database or
data.

8
00:01:03.780 --> 00:01:12.100
Small, reversible steps make a failed attempt
cheap, and the graph decides how often a step
may be retried.

9
00:01:13.500 --> 00:01:20.566
Reviews past or unfinished upgrade runs: what
was done, what is open and what went wrong.

10
00:01:21.916 --> 00:01:26.343
Git may say a branch is done while the run says
otherwise.

11
00:01:27.943 --> 00:01:32.266
Open source. Clone the skills, and help us
improve them.
